  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Sunday/...\nGuidance is starting to agree on a quicker drying trend later this\nweek as the Pacific trough is favored to move farther into the\nGreat Basin and at least into northern and western portions of the\nDesert Southwest. This is likely to push drier air eastward\nthrough most if not all of Arizona as early as Thursday but more\nso Friday into Saturday. Thursday is still a bit of an uncertain\nday as rain chances may still linger across the south-central\nlower deserts and definitely over eastern Arizona. However, by\nFriday, enough dry air moving in should end chances over the \nlower deserts and really limit chances over the high terrain. It \nis doubtful we will completely scour out all of the moisture \nacross the higher terrain, so 10-20% PoPs remain each day across \neastern Gila County through the weekend. \n\nAs conditions dry out into the weekend, temperatures are likely \nto face a bit of a warming trend but as of now the region is \nfavored to stay under broad upper level troughing into the \nweekend. Lower desert highs are expected to warm to above normal \nby Friday or Saturday, but so far the NBM indicates a most likely \nrange of 103-107 degrees.",
